-- index.md: Harbor (order 1)
<h1 id="harbor">Harbor<a class="headerlink" href="#harbor" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h1>
<p>Harbor is a self-hosted package registry for teams that want their own
mirror of the public indexes and a private place for internal packages.
It speaks the Python <em>simple</em> index, the npm registry protocol and a
plain HTTP file layout, so <code>pip</code>, <code>npm</code> and <code>curl</code> all work against it.</p>
<div class="toc">
<ul>
<li><a href="#why-harbor">Why Harbor</a></li>
<li><a href="#quick-start">Quick start</a></li>
<li><a href="#status">Status</a></li>
</ul>
</div>
<h2 id="why-harbor">Why Harbor<a class="headerlink" href="#why-harbor" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>One binary.</strong> No database server: metadata lives in an embedded
  store under <code>data_dir</code>, and blobs on disk or in an S3 bucket.</li>
<li><strong>Mirrors that keep working.</strong> A package you have installed once stays
  available when the upstream index is down &ndash; or when the author yanks it.</li>
<li><strong>Private packages.</strong> Publish with the tools you already use; see
  <a class="wikilink" href="/Publishing/">Publishing</a>.</li>
</ul>
<div class="admonition note">
<p class="admonition-title">Note</p>
<p>Harbor is not a build system. It stores what you give it and serves
it back, byte for byte.</p>
</div>
<h2 id="quick-start">Quick start<a class="headerlink" href="#quick-start" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<ol>
<li>Install the binary (see <a href="install.md">Installation</a>).</li>
<li>
<p>Write a two-line config:</p>
<p><code>toml
data_dir = "/var/lib/harbor"
listen = "127.0.0.1:7070"</code></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Run <code>harbor serve</code> and point <code>pip</code> at it:</p>
<pre class="codehilite"><code>pip install --index-url http://127.0.0.1:7070/pypi/simple/ requests
</code></pre>

</li>
</ol>
<h2 id="status">Status<a class="headerlink" href="#status" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th style="text-align: left;">Feature</th>
<th style="text-align: center;">Status</th>
<th style="text-align: right;">Since</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: left;">PyPI mirror</td>
<td style="text-align: center;">stable</td>
<td style="text-align: right;">0.4</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: left;">npm mirror</td>
<td style="text-align: center;">stable</td>
<td style="text-align: right;">0.6</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: left;">Private uploads</td>
<td style="text-align: center;">stable</td>
<td style="text-align: right;">0.7</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: left;">S3 blob store</td>
<td style="text-align: center;">beta</td>
<td style="text-align: right;">0.9</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style="text-align: left;">OCI images</td>
<td style="text-align: center;">not planned</td>
<td style="text-align: right;"></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Harbor&rsquo;s licence is the &ldquo;MIT&rdquo; licence<sup id="fnref:lic"><a class="footnote-ref" href="#fn:lic">1</a></sup>. It&rsquo;s been &ldquo;production ready&rdquo;
since &lsquo;23 &ndash; or so the changelog says&hellip;</p>
<div class="footnote">
<hr />
<ol>
<li id="fn:lic">
<p>See the <code>LICENSE</code> file in the source tree.&#160;<a class="footnote-backref" href="#fnref:lic" title="Jump back to footnote 1 in the text">&#8617;</a></p>
</li>
</ol>
</div>
