order: 1
summary: A self-hosted package registry for small teams.
title: Harbor
-- install.md: Installation (order 2)
<h1 id="install">Installation<a class="headerlink" href="#install" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h1>
<p>Harbor ships as a single static binary for Linux and macOS, and as a
container image.</p>
<h2 id="from-a-release">From a release<a class="headerlink" href="#from-a-release" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<p>Download the archive for your platform, check it, and put the binary on
your <code>PATH</code>:</p>
<pre class="codehilite"><code class="language-bash">curl -LO https://downloads.example.invalid/harbor/0.9.2/harbor-linux-x86_64.tar.gz
sha256sum -c harbor-0.9.2.sha256
tar xzf harbor-linux-x86_64.tar.gz
sudo install harbor /usr/local/bin/
</code></pre>

<div class="admonition warning">
<p class="admonition-title">Check the signature</p>
<p>The checksum file is signed. A checksum you downloaded from the same
place as the archive proves nothing on its own.</p>
</div>
<h2 id="with-a-container">With a container<a class="headerlink" href="#with-a-container" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<pre class="codehilite"><code>docker run -p 7070:7070 -v harbor-data:/data harbor/harbor:0.9.2
</code></pre>

<p>The image runs as user <code>harbor</code> (<abbr title="User identifier">uid</abbr> 10001) and keeps everything under
<code>/data</code>.</p>
<h2 class="advanced" id="from-source">From source<a class="headerlink" href="#from-source" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<p>You need a recent toolchain and <code>make</code>:</p>
<pre class="codehilite"><code class="language-shell">git clone https://git.example.invalid/harbor.git
cd harbor &amp;&amp; make release
</code></pre>
-- toc
<div class="toc">
<ul>
<li><a href="#from-a-release">From a release</a></li>
<li><a href="#with-a-container">With a container</a></li>
<li><a href="#from-source">From source</a></li>
</ul>
</div>

-- meta
order: 2
title: Installation
-- configuration.md: Configuration (order 3)
<h1 id="configuration">Configuration<a class="headerlink" href="#configuration" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h1>
<p>Harbor reads <code>harbor.toml</code> from the working directory, or the file named
by <code>--config</code>. Every key has a default; the smallest useful file names
only <code>data_dir</code>.</p>
<h2 id="keys">Keys<a class="headerlink" href="#keys" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<dl>
<dt><code>data_dir</code></dt>
<dd>Where the metadata store and the local blob store live. Required.</dd>
<dt><code>listen</code></dt>
<dd>The address to serve on. Default <code>127.0.0.1:7070</code>.</dd>
<dt><code>upstream.pypi</code></dt>
<dd>The index to mirror for Python packages. Default
<code>https://pypi.org/simple/</code>. Set it to <code>""</code> to turn the mirror off.</dd>
<dt><code>upstream.npm</code></dt>
<dd>
<p>The registry to mirror for npm packages.</p>
<p>Scoped packages (<code>@scope/name</code>) are mirrored too, unless the scope is
listed in <code>private_scopes</code>.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
<h2 id="blob-stores">Blob stores<a class="headerlink" href="#blob-stores" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<p>=== &ldquo;Disk&rdquo;
The default. Blobs are content-addressed files under <code>data_dir/blobs</code>.</p>
<div class="callout">
<p><strong>Tip:</strong> put <code>data_dir</code> on its own volume, so a full disk stops uploads
but not the operating system.</p>
</div>
<h3 id="s3">S3<a class="headerlink" href="#s3" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h3>
<pre class="codehilite"><code class="language-toml">[blobs]
kind = &quot;s3&quot;
bucket = &quot;harbor-blobs&quot;
region = &quot;eu-west-1&quot;
</code></pre>

<div class="admonition danger">
<p class="admonition-title">Credentials</p>
<p>Never write keys into <code>harbor.toml</code>. Harbor reads the usual
<code>AWS_*</code> environment variables, or the instance role.</p>
</div>
<h2 id="limits">Limits<a class="headerlink" href="#limits" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Limit</th>
<th>Default</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>max_upload</code></td>
<td>200 MiB</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>max_files</code></td>
<td>64</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>rate_per_min</code></td>
<td>120</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
-- toc
<div class="toc">
<ul>
<li><a href="#keys">Keys</a></li>
<li><a href="#blob-stores">Blob stores</a><ul>
<li><a href="#s3">S3</a></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><a href="#limits">Upload limits</a></li>
</ul>
</div>

