order: 3
title: Configuration
-- publishing.md: Publishing (order 4)
<h1 id="publishing-private-packages">Publishing private packages<a class="headerlink" href="#publishing-private-packages" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h1>
<p>Private packages live under a <em>namespace</em>. A namespace belongs to a team,
and only that team&rsquo;s tokens may upload to it.</p>
<h2 id="python">Python<a class="headerlink" href="#python" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<p>Build as usual, then upload with <code>twine</code>:</p>
<pre class="codehilite"><code class="language-shell">python -m build
twine upload --repository-url http://harbor.internal:7070/pypi/legacy/ dist/*
</code></pre>

<p>The first upload of a name <strong>claims</strong> it for the namespace. After that, an
upload from another team gets <code>403 Forbidden</code>.</p>
<h2 id="npm">npm<a class="headerlink" href="#npm" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<p>Point a scope at Harbor in <code>.npmrc</code>:</p>
<pre class="codehilite"><code>@acme:registry=http://harbor.internal:7070/npm/
</code></pre>

<p>and run <code>npm publish</code>. Unscoped private packages are not supported: an
unscoped name could shadow a public one.</p>
<h2 id="yanking">Yanking<a class="headerlink" href="#yanking" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<p>A yanked release stays downloadable by exact version, but <code>pip</code> and <code>npm</code>
will not pick it for a range. To yank:</p>
<ol>
<li>Open the release page, or</li>
<li>
<p>call the API:</p>
<p><code>http
POST /api/v1/releases/acme/widgets/1.4.0/yank HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code></p>
</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p>Yanking is for mistakes. To remove a release that leaked something,
<strong>delete</strong> it and rotate whatever leaked.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>See also <a class="wikilink" href="/Configuration/">Configuration</a> and <a href="api.md#releases">the API reference</a>.</p>
-- toc
<div class="toc">
<ul>
<li><a href="#python">Python</a></li>
<li><a href="#npm">npm</a></li>
<li><a href="#yanking">Yanking</a></li>
</ul>
</div>

-- meta
order: 4
title: Publishing
-- api.md: API (order 5)
<h1 id="http-api">HTTP API<a class="headerlink" href="#http-api" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h1>
<p>All endpoints live under <code>/api/v1/</code> and speak JSON. Authenticate with a
bearer token from <code>harbor token create</code>.</p>
<h2 id="packages">Packages<a class="headerlink" href="#packages" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<h3 id="get-apiv1packages"><code>GET /api/v1/packages</code><a class="headerlink" href="#get-apiv1packages" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h3>
<p>Lists packages, 50 to a page. Query parameters:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Name</th>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>q</code></td>
<td>string</td>
<td>Substring of the name</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>kind</code></td>
<td>string</td>
<td><code>pypi</code>, <code>npm</code> or <code>file</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>cursor</code></td>
<td>string</td>
<td>From the previous page&rsquo;s <code>next</code> field</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Response:</p>
<pre class="codehilite"><code class="language-json">{&quot;items&quot;: [{&quot;name&quot;: &quot;widgets&quot;, &quot;kind&quot;: &quot;pypi&quot;, &quot;latest&quot;: &quot;1.4.0&quot;}],
 &quot;next&quot;: null}
</code></pre>

<h2 id="releases">Releases<a class="headerlink" href="#releases" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<h3 id="post-apiv1releasesnsnameversionyank"><code>POST /api/v1/releases/{ns}/{name}/{version}/yank</code><a class="headerlink" href="#post-apiv1releasesnsnameversionyank" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h3>
<p>Marks a release yanked. Idempotent: yanking twice is not an error.</p>
<h3 id="delete-apiv1releasesnsnameversion"><code>DELETE /api/v1/releases/{ns}/{name}/{version}</code><a class="headerlink" href="#delete-apiv1releasesnsnameversion" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h3>
<p>Deletes the release and its files. <em>This cannot be undone.</em> Mirrors that
already fetched the files keep them.</p>
<h2 id="errors">Errors<a class="headerlink" href="#errors" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<p>Errors are <code>{"error": "&lt;code&gt;", "detail": "&lt;text&gt;"}</code> with an HTTP status:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>400</code> &ndash; <code>bad_request</code>: the body did not parse.</li>
<li><code>401</code> &ndash; <code>unauthorized</code>: no token, or an expired one.</li>
<li><code>403</code> &ndash; <code>forbidden</code>: the token&rsquo;s team does not own the namespace.</li>
<li><code>404</code> &ndash; <code>not_found</code>.</li>
<li><code>409</code> &ndash; <code>conflict</code>: the version already exists.</li>
</ul>
<details>
<summary>Retry advice</summary>
Retry `429` and `503` with backoff; never retry a `409`.
</details>
-- toc
<div class="toc">
<ul>
<li><a href="#packages">Packages</a><ul>
<li><a href="#get-apiv1packages">GET /api/v1/packages</a></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><a href="#releases">Releases</a><ul>
<li><a href="#post-apiv1releasesnsnameversionyank">POST /api/v1/releases/{ns}/{name}/{version}/yank</a></li>
<li><a href="#delete-apiv1releasesnsnameversion">DELETE /api/v1/releases/{ns}/{name}/{version}</a></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><a href="#errors">Errors</a></li>
</ul>
</div>

