order: 5
title: API
-- faq.md: FAQ (order 6)
<h1 id="frequently-asked-questions">Frequently asked questions<a class="headerlink" href="#frequently-asked-questions" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h1>
<h2 id="does-harbor-proxy-requests-it-cannot-serve">Does Harbor proxy requests it cannot serve?<a class="headerlink" href="#does-harbor-proxy-requests-it-cannot-serve" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<p>Yes. A request for a file Harbor does not have goes upstream once; the
answer is stored and every later request is served locally.</p>
<h2 id="can-i-run-two-harbors-behind-a-load-balancer">Can I run two Harbors behind a load balancer?<a class="headerlink" href="#can-i-run-two-harbors-behind-a-load-balancer" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<p>Not yet. The metadata store takes a lock on <code>data_dir</code>, so a second
process on the same directory exits with:</p>
<pre class="codehilite"><code>error: data_dir /var/lib/harbor is locked by pid 4242
</code></pre>

<h2 id="how-big-does-data_dir-get">How big does <code>data_dir</code> get?<a class="headerlink" href="#how-big-does-data_dir-get" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<p>Roughly the size of everything ever installed through it, plus about 2%
for metadata. Run <code>harbor gc --dry-run</code> to see what a clean-up would
free.</p>
<h2 id="why-harbor">Why &ldquo;Harbor&rdquo;?<a class="headerlink" href="#why-harbor" title="Permanent link">&para;</a></h2>
<p>Because packages come in, get stored, and go out again. Also, the
author&rsquo;s previous project was called &ldquo;Dock&rdquo; and the joke wrote itself.</p>
-- toc
<div class="toc">
<ul>
<li><a href="#does-harbor-proxy-requests-it-cannot-serve">Does Harbor proxy requests it cannot serve?</a></li>
<li><a href="#can-i-run-two-harbors-behind-a-load-balancer">Can I run two Harbors behind a load balancer?</a></li>
<li><a href="#how-big-does-data_dir-get">How big does data_dir get?</a></li>
<li><a href="#why-harbor">Why &ldquo;Harbor&rdquo;?</a></li>
</ul>
</div>

